    {
      "id": "p0132-b013",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In the English version of Undertale, Snowdin's inn is aptly named the \"Snowed Inn\". Toby knew this pun would likely be lost in translation, so he suggested an alternative name: \"Snowtel\". The translator agreed that this combination of the English words \"snow\" and \"hotel\" would be more recognizable to Japanese players. However, this change also meant that that English-speaking players and Japanese-speaking players would know the same place by a different name.",
        "raw": "In the English version of Undertale, Snowdin's inn is aptly named the \"Snowed\nInn\". Toby knew this pun would likely be lost in translation, so he suggested\nan alternative name: \"Snowtel\". The translator agreed that this combination of\nthe English words \"snow\" and \"hotel\" would be more recognizable to Japanese\nplayers. However, this change also meant that that English-speaking players\nand Japanese-speaking players would know the same place by a different name.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
